Bugfix: Add accessible names to the remaining select2 pickers and storage fields

The group picker in the admin sharing settings, the "Available for" user/group
picker of an external storage and the runtime-generated storage configuration
fields (host, user name, password, ...) had no accessible name. Screen readers
announced an unlabeled text box, and the configuration fields relied on their
placeholder alone, which is not a name and disappears as soon as something is
typed.

The pickers follow the pattern already used in the sharing settings: select2
copies the text of label[for=<id>] into the offscreen label of the search field
it builds, so a matching label element is what names the widget. Where a control
exists once per storage row a fixed id would be present several times in the
document, so those controls carry an aria-label instead. The rendered layout is
unchanged.

WCAG 2.1 AA, SC 3.3.2, SC 4.1.2, SC 1.3.1
